# __DISPLAY_NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

## Develop

```bash
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests
cupcake-plugin-dev validate
cupcake-plugin-dev docs --write
cupcake-plugin-dev package
```

`package` checks the plugin the way CUPCAKE checks an upload and writes `dist/__PLUGIN_NAME__-<version>.tar.gz`.

## Install

On a CUPCAKE appliance, open Cupcake › Admin › Plugins and choose the package. CUPCAKE installs it,
registers it on a local port, writes its settings and starts it. Settings can be changed afterwards in
`/etc/cupcake/plugins/__PLUGIN_NAME__.env`.

Only the CUPCAKE backend calls the plugin. Every endpoint except `/health` requires the callback key the
backend sends during the startup handshake.

## Run it locally

```bash
PLUGIN_TOKEN=<token> CUPCAKE_BACKEND=http://localhost:8000 python3 plugin.py
```

Register the plugin first with `POST /api/v1/plugins/register/` as staff to get the token.

